This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

<tools-used-before-summary>AskUserQuestion, Bash, Edit, Monitor, Read, Skill, TaskStop, ToolSearch, Write, mcp__mi-feishu__fetch-doc, mcp__mi-feishu__update-doc</tools-used-before-summary>
Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   - **Governing intent (from earlier turns, still binding):** verify every function SUCCEEDS on the real BK7258 board, not failure branches. Earlier verbatim: "我是要走功能测试都成功的路径，不是'（未联网 → E1/E2 分支）'…请你拟订个'功能测试成功'sh脚本，我们先把功能验证好了，再去验证'流程+功能'出现预定情况的正确性".
   - **Interaction style (explicit correction, still binding):** "执行到什么就显示什么，要求我做什么，不要预先把之后的流程一并打印出来…而且pc上不要用通知弹窗的形式通知我，就用claude的checkpoint形式，在会话终端问我" — drive one step at a time; announce only the current step/current key; no notify-send/desktop popups; no upfront plan dumps.
   - **Script ownership:** "不要自己擅自创建流程脚本和文本，我要求创建时再创建" — only create scripts/docs when explicitly asked (`yzhang/testLoop/func-test.sh` and `run-ui-flow.sh` are user-owned).
   - **Current driving request (from just before compaction):** "ok，现在逐项逐项验证功能，注意要真实功能，不要注入虚假验证" — verify each func-test item one by one using REAL functionality: no `notify_inject`, no `rpending` simulated approval, no `fake-*` models, no fake backend. Real LLM, real ACP backend, real tool-permission approval, real Gerrit/Jira notifications, real mic/ASR/TTS.
   - **Newest explicit request:** "还是报'语音识别不可用，请检查网络和语音识别配置'，你修复一下音频采集" — fix audio capture so voice works.
   - **Standing security/operational constraints (must persist verbatim in effect):**
     - Never echo secret values from `yzhang/cmd_scripts.sh` — cite **line numbers only** (Wi-Fi 33/39, DNS 47, LLM key 50, Volc key 56, voice self-test 59-60, Gerrit token 69, Jira PAT 70, remote broker/auth 105-106). The board echoes commands it receives, so secret-bearing lines must have their **echo masked** in captured output; do not print raw serial output in the same command that sends line 106 (a Bash call was previously DENIED by the auto-mode classifier for "Credential Materialization").
     - The LLM API key, the Gerrit gateway token, **and the MQTT broker username/password from cmd_scripts.sh:106** are treated as exposed and should be rotated.
     - Redact `sk-…` and any ≥24-char token before writing logs; contest-repo log sync must be redacted (skill `contest-log-redact`).
     - Never type bare `reboot` in BK7258 NSH (only `reboot bootloader`); never type `quit` in `vela>` (use `restart`); never `kill -9` the qemu emulator.
     - Flashing is destructive: requires explicit authorization + announcing device and complete SHA-256 immediately before an interactive (never backgrounded) launch.
     - `~/桌面/实验计划书_ai_agent全功能验证与录制_20260920.md` §2 and `~/桌面/tmp/key.txt` must never enter the repo, logs, or output.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - BK7258 dual-core: UI/LVGL on AP (armino-style); AP console `/dev/ttyUSB0` (CH340 1a86:7523); CP consoles `/dev/ttyACM0/1` (1a86:55d3, ttyACM1 currently held by the user's minicom). Prompts `nsh-ap>` and `vela>`; `restart` at vela> → `nsh-ap>`.
   - AP `/data` is tmpfs → every reboot/reset loses all config (Wi-Fi, set_dns, set_llm, set_volc_key, set_remote/auth, MCP); must re-provision.
   - func-test.sh phases (all real except approval/notify): `net start config text voice keys approval notify`; `./func-test.sh net start config` re-provisions Wi-Fi/DNS/LLM/Volc keys from cmd_scripts.sh by line number without displaying content.
   - Real ACP backend: mimo 0.1.14 at `/home/zhangy101/.mimocode/bin/mimo` (not on PATH), `mimo acp --pure` (adapter adds `--pure` automatically); kiro-cli exists but "Not logged in". ACP supports `session/new` returning `models.currentModelId` + `availableModels`, and `session/set_model` actually switches the backend model.
   - Device remote protocol: `hello/hello_ack`, `snapshot`, `models`, `session_list`, `prompt_submit`; device→bridge `model_select`, `session_new`, `session_switch`. Device only sends `hello` after a fresh MQTT connect; restarting the bridge requires re-running `set_remote` to force a re-handshake. `remote_codec_build_session_switch` accepts digits only; `rstat` prints `Session : gen%s`.
   - `REMOTE_MODEL_MAX 64`, `REMOTE_MODEL_OPTIONS_MAX 32` (remote_link.h).
   - Audio architecture on AP: `packages/ai_agent/src/voice/{audio_capture.c,voice_channel.c,ptt_button.c,volc_asr.c,...}` + NuttX audio lower half `chips/bk7258/audio/{bk7258_audio.c,bk7258_adc.c,bk7258_dac.c,bk7258_gdma.c}`, device `/dev/audio/pcm0c` (capture) and `/dev/audio/pcm0p` (playback).
   - Playback proven working (TTS audible; `[audio_pb] backend: nuttx direct`), TTS REST v3 and batch ASR over HTTPS work; streaming ASR (WSS) fails TLS handshake `-0x004c` → falls back to batch.
   - Known pre-existing faults: LVGL thread can wedge holding `lvgl_ui_lock` during `ask` reply bubbles (recovery = K1 reset); CH340 `/dev/ttyUSB0` can go fully silent while the board still runs (recovery = replug USB); standby swallows the first key press.

3. Files and Code Sections:
   - **`contest2026_272_tokenwujixian/tools/acp-bridge/src/acp-adapter.js`** (edited — makes model switch REAL):
     - Constructor additions:
       ```js
       this.availableModels = [];
       this.modelId = null;
       ```
     - `start()` now calls `this.#syncModels(created);` after `this.sessionId = created.sessionId;` and before emitting `session_started`.
     - `newSession()` now re-applies the chosen model:
       ```js
       const wanted = this.modelId;
       this.#syncModels(created);
       if (wanted && wanted !== this.modelId) {
         try { await this.setModel(wanted); } catch { /* keep the backend default */ }
       }
       this.listener({ type: "session_started", backend: this.backend, sessionId: this.sessionId });
       ```
     - New methods:
       ```js
       #syncModels(created) {
         const models = created?.models;
         if (!models || typeof models !== "object") return;
         if (typeof models.currentModelId === "string" && models.currentModelId) this.modelId = models.currentModelId;
         if (!Array.isArray(models.availableModels)) return;
         const seen = new Set(); const options = [];
         for (const entry of models.availableModels) {
           const id = entry?.modelId;
           if (typeof id !== "string" || !id) continue;
           if (/\/(low|medium|high|xhigh|max)$/.test(id)) continue;
           if (seen.has(id)) continue;
           seen.add(id); options.push(id);
         }
         if (options.length === 0) return;
         if (this.modelId && seen.has(this.modelId)) {
           options.splice(options.indexOf(this.modelId), 1);
           options.unshift(this.modelId);
         }
         this.availableModels = options;
         this.listener({ type: "models", current: this.modelId, options });
       }
       async setModel(modelId) {
         const result = await this.request("session/set_model", { sessionId: this.sessionId, modelId });
         this.modelId = modelId;
         this.listener({ type: "models", current: modelId, options: this.availableModels });
         return result;
       }
