   - Audio capture chain: `/dev/audio/pcm0c` → `chips/bk7258/audio/bk7258_audio.c` (capture half) → `bk7258_adc.c` / `bk7258_gdma.c`. ADC FIFO `AUD_ADC_FPORT` emits one 32-bit word per sample period: `[31:16]=ADCR`, `[15:0]=ADCL`; DMA must move 32-bit words whole; DMA buffer therefore holds interleaved stereo frames that must be compacted to 16-bit mono (ADCL) for the upper half, which advertises 16 kHz/16-bit/1ch.
   - Vendor ground truth: `bk_avdk_smp/ap/components/bk_audio/audio_streams/onboard_mic_stream/onboard_mic_stream.c` — `frame_size` doubling for chl_num==1 and `_onboard_mic_read()`'s "remove adcr data and remain adcl data" loop `ptr[i] = ptr[2*i]`, then `ret = ret/2`.
   - ARMv8-M cache: `up_invalidate_dcache` uses `NVIC_DCIMVAC` (discard dirty lines) for interior lines and `NVIC_DCCIMVAC` (clean+invalidate) for a partial head line — hence ISR compaction must be followed by `up_clean_dcache` or the reader's later invalidate would drop the compacted data.
   - Volc ASR v3 streaming: server replies with a final frame whose text may be empty when its VAD hears no speech; `-61`/`-ENODATA` = no text. Request JSON `audio{format=pcm,codec=raw,rate=16000,bits=16,channel=1}`, `request{model_name:bigmodel,…}`.
   - Agent dispatch: `agent_main.c: outbound_dispatch_task()` routes by `msg.channel`; `AGENT_CHAN_VOICE` speaks only; `AGENT_CHAN_LVGL_UI` renders + speaks; `"cli"` prints `[agent] reply N bytes` and mirrors to LVGL. On AP the LVGL build's `lvgl_ui_channel_send()` = async bubble creation + `voice_channel_speak()` (when network connected).
   - Build/flash tooling: skill `bk7258-worktree-build` wrapper `full_flow.sh` (computed slot `cmake_out/bk7258-worktrees/contest2026_272_tokenwujixian--49c79c3da11c`); `--flash` must run in a real foreground TTY (tmux session `bkflash-1027`), never piped/redirected; it auto-injects `reboot bootloader` (AON-WDT chip reset).
   - Diagnostics: `apps/testing/bk7258_pcm` built-in (`-N` driver read path with `[bk-N] samples=… pp=… LIVE`, `-C` direct FIFO dual-channel probe that always captures ~1 s per XTAL/APLL phase regardless of `-d`, `-T/-F/-M/-L`); NSH builtins available: `hexdump xd wget cat dd cp nxplayer nxrecorder sh ps free df`; NSH built-ins share task statics across invocations.
   - `bk7258_pcm` sets its own volume/gain (vol=20 log line) and reads the ADC with default gain 0x2D; the agent path applies ×6 software gain after read.

